Fillets: a radius law of the caller's along a contour (mitcad#464).

BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet::SetRadius(Law_Function, IC, IinC) is meant to
give a contour's rounding the radius the law gives at each parameter of
its spine, but ChFiDS_FilSpine::SetRadius put the law in a composite it
then dropped and cleared the radii set at points, so the contour was left
with no radius at all. The other variable radii are interpolated through
(parameter, radius) points with level ends (Law_Interpol), so a radius
given as a B-spline of the position along the edges (Mitcad's spline
fillet radius) could only be approximated through them.

ChFiDS_FilSpine keeps the law now (`userlaw`, by the spine's parameter,
the abscissa from its first vertex). ComputeLaw gives each guideline the
law over its range, constant at the law's end values where the guideline
runs past the law's bounds (an extension at an end); a closed contour with
a law is refused. The spine with a law is not constant on any edge
(IsConstant, Radius), its largest radius is sampled from the law
(MaxRadFromSeqAndLaws), Reset keeps it (and does not complete the radii
at points, which it has none of), and a radius set at a point, or a reset
of all data, drops it.

